I built the C library with CMake, wrote three C harnesses that declare the prototypes directly, and linked each harness twice — once against [38;5;10mlibharvest-work-JSWavh.so[0m, once against [38;5;10mlibharvest_translation.so[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- harness 1 (1345 lines): every exported function; hash vectors across lengths 0–40 and five seeds; array growth; binary and string maps with 300/200 keys plus deletes and re-lookups; [38;5;10mstrdup[0m and arena modes; direct arena use; NULL-argument paths; [38;5;10mhelxo[0m.[0m[0m
- harness 2 (1917 lines): reads the internal [38;5;10mstbds_hash_index[0m through a layout-compatible struct — [38;5;10mslot_count[0m, thresholds, [38;5;10mtombstone_count[0m, [38;5;10mseed[0m, [38;5;10mslot_count_log2[0m, arena state, [38;5;10mtemp_key[0m, and 64-byte [38;5;10mstorage[0m alignment — across 1000-key insert/delete cycles that trigger table growth, shrink and tombstone rebuild. Also 4 KB hash inputs, odd element sizes, and the table-seed LCG progression.[0m[0m
- harness 3: [38;5;10mhelxo[0m with [38;5;10m\0[0m, [38;5;10m0x80[0m, [38;5;10m0xff[0m, [38;5;10m\t[0m, [38;5;10m%[0m.[0m[0m
