[38;5;252m[1m## Behaviours reproduced rather than fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- **Sign extension in [38;5;10mstbds_siphash_bytes[0m.** [38;5;10md[0] | (d[1]<<8) | (d[2]<<16) | (d[3]<<24)[0m is an [38;5;10mint[0m expression assigned to [38;5;10msize_t[0m, so a byte ≥ 0x80 at [38;5;10md[3][0m sign-extends and floods the high 32 bits of [38;5;10mdata[0m. Same for [38;5;10mcase 4:[0m in the tail switch. Rust reproduces this via [38;5;10m(lo as i32) as isize as usize[0m; the all-[38;5;10m0x80[0m/all-[38;5;10m0xff[0m vectors in harness 1 pin it down.[0m[0m
- **[38;5;10mhash ^= hash ^ ROR(hash,n)[0m** in [38;5;10mstbds_hash_string[0m, which reduces to a plain rotate, written literally.[0m[0m
